From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:07:12 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 72/74] Plutonium: app icons in the switcher's window list and
 launcher

PlutoniumAppIcons gets an app's icon from the helper (GET /v1/apps/<id>/icon,
which also takes a window's app id) and decodes it, PNG or SVG, in a
background about:blank WebContents with DownloadImage, as Chrome's Almanac
icon loader does: an SVG needs a renderer. The decoder goes after 30 s idle.
The helper client gains GetBytes for answers that aren't JSON. Window rows show
the icon beside their state dot; the launcher's rows show it instead of the
dot.
